{
  "manufacturer": "Eaton",
  "manufacturer_slug": "eaton",
  "model": "S611 soft starter (via C441 Ethernet module)",
  "model_slug": "s611-soft-starter",
  "short_model": "S611",
  "aliases": [
    "S611",
    "S611 soft starter",
    "C441R",
    "C441T"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Soft starter",
  "applies_to": "Eaton S611 soft starters read through a C441R or C441T plug-in Ethernet module, per Table 98 of MN04200002E.",
  "summary": "The S611 is an Eaton soft starter with built-in motor protection and metering. Through the C441 Ethernet module its data is served over Modbus TCP and RS-485 Modbus RTU. This map covers adapter I/O and comms registers, motor status and metering (300-338), the run/permissive/reset control word (400) and the start, protection and comm-loss settings (401-445).",
  "transport": [
    "TCP",
    "RTU",
    "ASCII"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Tables print register numbers starting at 1; the manual states that the Modbus register address is the register number minus 1 (field inputs, register 1, is address 0)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "C441 Ethernet Module User Manual (C441R, C441T, C441U, C441V)",
    "doc_number": "MN04200002E",
    "revision_date": "2012-08",
    "url": "https://www.precision-elec.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/C441-Ethernet-Module-User-Manual-C441R-C441T-C441U-C441V.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 56-59 (section 7.4, Table 98)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Source is a distributor copy (precision-elec.com) of Eaton manual MN04200002E dated August 2012. Eaton lists a later edition (January 2016) at eaton.com, which could not be downloaded from this machine; check it for changes.",
    "The tables print 1-based Modbus register numbers: the production/consumption-list note says field inputs register 1 is register address 0 (address = register number - 1).",
    "All registers listed are single 16-bit words. Multi-word items (32-bit adapter serial number at 7, firmware/hardware revision at 9/11, IP addresses 144-154, MAC address 156) have no stated word order or layout and are left out. Signedness is not stated; values are typed unsigned.",
    "The same map is served over Modbus TCP and over the adapter's RS-485 Modbus RTU port; functions 01/02/03/04/05/06/15/16/23 and 43/14 are supported. Coil numbers in the manual are bit views of the same registers and are not listed here.",
    "Registers 1000-4000 are a user-configurable production/consumption list (custom register block); not expanded here.",
    "Currents 302-305 must be divided using the current scale factor in register 301 (the manual does not define the factor further), so they are left unscaled here.",
    "Fault code 325 starts a fault queue read newest first.",
    "Firmware registers 335/336 and the change-tracker queue 399 are left out (no description in the manual); command code 250 is marked unpublished and left out.",
    "Defaults are those printed for the C441R/C441T serial monitoring port (address 1, 19.2k, even parity, 1 stop bit, RTU); data bits and the Modbus TCP port are not stated.",
    "Residual ground fault current 317 and trip level 419 are printed as 'Scaling = x100' with no unit; they are scaled 0.01 here and the unit is left blank."
  ],
